[statement]
Before a name some package carries is decided, a name whose one
candidate depends on a name a candidate of it provides is decided too, not
only one depending on the carried name itself: `px`, required by `app`,
provides `x3`, which `kw`, the one candidate for `w`, needs. `w` is
decided first, and `kw` answers `v`, which `app` lists first, so `gk` is
not installed. Contrast `a-sole-candidate-without-a-real-dependency-waits`.

[repository]
P:app
V:1
D:v w px

P:kw
V:1
D:x3
p:v w=1

P:px
V:1
p:x3=1

P:gk
V:1
k:100
p:v

[request]
app

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install px 1
install kw 1
install app 1
